(13. AI Interaction Design) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(| Topic | Rule |) Tj
T*
(|---|---|) Tj
T*
(| How AI appears | As explainable assistants, inline summaries, recommendation rationale, evidence analysis, and ) Tj
T*
(roadmap suggestions. |) Tj
T*
(| When AI speaks | When it can cite evidence, explain uncertainty, and propose an action. |) Tj
T*
(| When AI remains silent | When evidence is insufficient, privacy is unclear, or answer would be speculative/high-) Tj
T*
(impact without review. |) Tj
T*
(| Explainability UX | Always show "Why?" and "Evidence" affordances near recommendations and capability claims. |) Tj
T*
(| Confidence UX | Use bands and plain-language labels; avoid false precision as primary display. |) Tj
T*
(| Evidence UX | Evidence cards show source, date, type, strength, confidence impact, and provenance. |) Tj
T*
(| Recommendation UX | Recommendation cards include reason, expected impact, effort, confidence, and alternatives. |) Tj
T*
(| Conversation UX | AI chat is scoped to current context and cannot invent claims. It should say when evidence is ) Tj
T*
(missing. |) Tj
T*
(| Inline suggestions | Use subtle cards/chips, not intrusive modals. |) Tj
T*
(| Feedback collection | Users can mark useful/not useful, dispute, add context, or request human review. |) Tj
T*
(| Trust indicators | Verified, human-reviewed, AI-assisted, stale, disputed, revoked, and jurisdiction-specific ) Tj
T*
(badges. |) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(AI must never appear magical. It should behave like an evidence-aware guide.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(14. Design Principles) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(| Principle | Specification |) Tj
T*
(|---|---|) Tj
T*
(| Typography | Modern, readable, premium; generous line height; tabular numerals for metrics. |) Tj
T*
(| Spacing | Calm spacing, strong grouping, avoid dense admin clutter on student surfaces. |) Tj
T*
(| Information density | Progressive disclosure: summary -> explanation -> evidence -> provenance. |) Tj
T*
(| Color | Neutral enterprise palette; accent colors for capability, evidence, confidence, risk. Avoid red/green-only ) Tj
T*
(meaning. |) Tj
T*
(| Accessibility | WCAG AA baseline; semantic HTML; visible focus; screen reader labels. |) Tj
T*
(| Motion | Subtle and purposeful; no distracting animation in analytical views. |) Tj
T*
(| Loading states | Skeletons for cards/tables; explicit AI processing states with cancel/retry. |) Tj
T*
(| Error states | Explain what failed, why it matters, and how to recover. |) Tj
T*
(| Empty states | Teach next action and explain why data is missing. |) Tj
T*
(| Micro-interactions | Evidence expand, confidence tooltip, copy/share, save filters. |) Tj
T*
(| Dark mode | Premium dark mode for dashboards; preserve contrast and chart readability. |) Tj
T*
(| Light mode | Default for institutional and student use. |) Tj
T*
(| Enterprise appearance | Trustworthy, restrained, data-rich but not cluttered. |) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
